# This board needs btd paused while a gamepad bonds.
#
# robotctl reads only whether this file exists; the text is for whoever finds it.
# Shipped by the microduck-daemon recipe (TEMPORARY, remove-with-real-radio),
# where scripts/setup-board.sh --pause-btd-on-pair would write it on Armbian.
#
# It says nothing about Privacy. This image also sets Privacy = device in
# /etc/bluetooth/main.conf, from meta-microduck's bluez5 bbappend -- the pair of
# them is what provision-board.sh --weird-ble does.
#
# A workaround for the AIC8800 radio, which is not what ships. Delete this file
# to stop pausing btd; delete the bbappend to drop Privacy = device. Both go,
# with BtdPaused in robotctl, when the real radio lands.
